Finalized Change Request: Upload Certificate to Airship Portal (NA iOS) 
Short Description 
Upload Certificate to Airship portal NA iOS – expires on 09/28/2025 
Description 
Upload the new certificate to the Airship portal for NA iOS. The current certificate expires on 
09/28/2025. Failure to update will impact Wallet services due to insecure connections, potentially 
causing service downtime and user inconvenience. 
Justification 
The Airship portal certificate for NA iOS is expiring on 09/28/2025. Timely renewal is essential to 
maintain secure connections and uninterrupted Wallet service functionality. 
Configuration Item 
Mobile App iOS NA 
CMDB Update Required? 
No 
Risk and Impact 
Risk Level: Moderate 
Impact: Expiration of the certificate will disrupt secure connections, leading to service downtime 
and operational interruptions for Wallet services. 
Approval 
CAB Approval required 
Status 
Draft 
Planned Dates examples  
• Start Date: 2025-09-16 14:00:00 
• End Date: 2025-09-16 18:00:00 
• Test Start Date: 2025-09-09 10:00:00 
• Test End Date: 2025-09-11 10:00:00 
Implementation Plan 
1. Log in to Airship portal 
2. Click on NA prod certificate 
3. Navigate to Settings > Certificates in the Airship portal. 
4. Go to Project Certificates. 
5. Select iOS and click Replace Certificate. 
6. Choose Upload a new .p12. 
7. Enter the certificate password (attached). 
8. Click Choose File and upload the new certificate. 
9. Click Save. 
Backout Plan 
• Approach 1: Revert to the existing certificate (expiring on 07/28/2024). 
• Approach 2: Generate a new .p12 certificate and replace again if needed. 
Post Deployment Validation Plan 
1. Verify the updated expiry date in the Airship portal. 
2. Order a test cookie to validate ordering flows for:  
o Instore 
o Curbside 
o Delivery 
(NA region only) all 3 regions ( US, CA and PR) 
